[{"role": "system", "content": "\nYou are a programming expert. \nYou will be provided with a patch used to fix a bug. \n\nYour task is summarize the modifications made in the patch.\nYour summary should consist of two parts, modifications in each file and their relationships.\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "From 003b686ace820ce2d635a83f10f2d7f9c147dabc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: YueHaibing <yuehaibing@huawei.com>\nDate: Tue, 12 Mar 2019 15:03:58 +0800\nSubject: [PATCH] mwifiex: Fix mem leak in mwifiex_tm_cmd\n\n'hostcmd' is alloced by kzalloc, should be freed before\nleaving from the error handling cases, otherwise it will\ncause mem leak.\n\nFixes: 3935ccc14d2c (\"mwifiex: add cfg80211 testmode support\")\nSigned-off-by: YueHaibing <yuehaibing@huawei.com>\nSigned-off-by: Kalle Valo <kvalo@codeaurora.org>\n\ndiff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cfg80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cfg80211.c\nindex c46f0a54a0c7..e582d9b3e50c 100644\n--- a/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cfg80211.c\n+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cfg80211.c\n@@ -4082,16 +4082,20 @@ static int mwifiex_tm_cmd(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct wireless_dev *wdev,\n \n \t\tif (mwifiex_send_cmd(priv, 0, 0, 0, hostcmd, true)) {\n \t\t\tdev_err(priv->adapter->dev, \"Failed to process hostcmd\\n\");\n+\t\t\tkfree(hostcmd);\n \t\t\treturn -EFAULT;\n \t\t}\n \n \t\t/* process hostcmd response*/\n \t\tskb = cfg80211_testmode_alloc_reply_skb(wiphy, hostcmd->len);\n-\t\tif (!skb)\n+\t\tif (!skb) {\n+\t\t\tkfree(hostcmd);\n \t\t\treturn -ENOMEM;\n+\t\t}\n \t\terr = nla_put(skb, MWIFIEX_TM_ATTR_DATA,\n \t\t\t      hostcmd->len, hostcmd->cmd);\n \t\tif (err) {\n+\t\t\tkfree(hostcmd);\n \t\t\tkfree_skb(skb);\n \t\t\treturn -EMSGSIZE;\n \t\t}\n-- \n2.25.1\n\n\n\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "### Modifications in Each File\n\n**File: `drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cfg80211.c`**\n1. Added `kfree(hostcmd);` before returning from the error handling cases where the `hostcmd` allocation fails or when processing the command fails.\n2. The modifications ensure that the memory allocated for `hostcmd` is properly freed in three different error scenarios:\n   - When `mwifiex_send_cmd` fails.\n   - When `cfg80211_testmode_alloc_reply_skb` fails.\n   - When `nla_put` fails.\n\n### Relationships Between Modifications\nThe modifications are related in that they all address the same issue: preventing a memory leak by ensuring that the allocated memory for `hostcmd` is freed in all error handling paths. This is crucial for maintaining memory integrity and preventing resource exhaustion in the system. Each added `kfree(hostcmd);` statement corresponds to a specific failure point in the command processing flow, ensuring that no matter where the function exits due to an error, the allocated memory is released."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"llm_patch_file_names": ["drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cfg80211.c"]}, "begin to deal with drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cfg80211.c in strategy1", {"full_context_length": 64}, {"role": "system", "content": "You are a programming expert."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\n        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.\n        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.\n\n        Root cause:\n        The bug is caused by the failure to free the memory allocated for `hostcmd` in various error handling paths within the `mwifiex_tm_cmd` function. When `hostcmd` is allocated using `kzalloc`, it must be freed if any subsequent operations fail, otherwise it leads to a memory leak.\n        \n        Commit message:\n        mwifiex: Fix mem leak in mwifiex_tm_cmd\n\n'hostcmd' is alloced by kzalloc, should be freed before\nleaving from the error handling cases, otherwise it will\ncause mem leak.\n\nFixes: 3935ccc14d2c (\"mwifiex: add cfg80211 testmode support\")\nSigned-off-by: YueHaibing <yuehaibing@huawei.com>\nSigned-off-by: Kalle Valo <kvalo@codeaurora.org>  \n        \n        Patch:\n         \n static int mwifiex_tm_cmd(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct wireless_dev *wdev,\n \t\t\t  void *data, int len)\n {\n \tstruct mwifiex_private *priv = mwifiex_netdev_get_priv(wdev->netdev);\n \tstruct mwifiex_ds_misc_cmd *hostcmd;\n \tstruct nlattr *tb[MWIFIEX_TM_ATTR_MAX + 1];\n \tstruct sk_buff *skb;\n \tint err;\n \n \tif (!priv)\n \t\treturn -EINVAL;\n \n \terr = nla_parse(tb, MWIFIEX_TM_ATTR_MAX, data, len, mwifiex_tm_policy,\n \t\t\tNULL);\n \tif (err)\n \t\treturn err;\n \n \tif (!tb[MWIFIEX_TM_ATTR_CMD])\n \t\treturn -EINVAL;\n \n \tswitch (nla_get_u32(tb[MWIFIEX_TM_ATTR_CMD])) {\n \tcase MWIFIEX_TM_CMD_HOSTCMD:\n \t\tif (!tb[MWIFIEX_TM_ATTR_DATA])\n \t\t\treturn -EINVAL;\n \n \t\thostcmd = kzalloc(sizeof(*hostcmd), GFP_KERNEL);\n \t\tif (!hostcmd)\n \t\t\treturn -ENOMEM;\n \n \t\thostcmd->len = nla_len(tb[MWIFIEX_TM_ATTR_DATA]);\n \t\tmemcpy(hostcmd->cmd, nla_data(tb[MWIFIEX_TM_ATTR_DATA]),\n \t\t       hostcmd->len);\n \n \t\tif (mwifiex_send_cmd(priv, 0, 0, 0, hostcmd, true)) {\n \t\t\tdev_err(priv->adapter->dev, \"Failed to process hostcmd\\n\");\n+\t\t\tkfree(hostcmd);\n \t\t\treturn -EFAULT;\n \t\t}\n \n \t\t/* process hostcmd response*/\n \t\tskb = cfg80211_testmode_alloc_reply_skb(wiphy, hostcmd->len);\n-\t\tif (!skb)\n+\t\tif (!skb) {\n+\t\t\tkfree(hostcmd);\n \t\t\treturn -ENOMEM;\n+\t\t}\n \t\terr = nla_put(skb, MWIFIEX_TM_ATTR_DATA,\n \t\t\t      hostcmd->len, hostcmd->cmd);\n \t\tif (err) {\n+\t\t\tkfree(hostcmd);\n \t\t\tkfree_skb(skb);\n \t\t\treturn -EMSGSIZE;\n \t\t}\n \n \t\terr = cfg80211_testmode_reply(skb);\n \t\tkfree(hostcmd);\n \t\treturn err;\n \tdefault:\n \t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n \t}\n }\n #endif\n\n        \n        Provide a response strictly in the following format:\n        Code statements:\n        <text1>\n        <text2>\n        ...\n        <textN>\n    "}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Code statements:\n```c\nhostcmd = kzalloc(sizeof(*hostcmd), GFP_KERNEL);\nif (!hostcmd)\n    return -ENOMEM;\n\nif (mwifiex_send_cmd(priv, 0, 0, 0, hostcmd, true)) {\n    dev_err(priv->adapter->dev, \"Failed to process hostcmd\\n\");\n    kfree(hostcmd);\n    return -EFAULT;\n}\n\nskb = cfg80211_testmode_alloc_reply_skb(wiphy, hostcmd->len);\nif (!skb) {\n    kfree(hostcmd);\n    return -ENOMEM;\n}\n\nif (err) {\n    kfree(hostcmd);\n    kfree_skb(skb);\n    return -EMSGSIZE;\n}\n\n\tkfree(hostcmd);\n```"}, {"s1_raw_stmts_infos": [{"buggy_stmt": "hostcmd = kzalloc(sizeof(*hostcmd), GFP_KERNEL);", "file_name": "drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cfg80211.c", "lineno": 4075, "induce_cid": "3935ccc14d2c68488bd96448fc073da48eaeebf0"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (!hostcmd)", "file_name": "drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cfg80211.c", "lineno": 4076, "induce_cid": "3935ccc14d2c68488bd96448fc073da48eaeebf0"}, {"buggy_stmt": "return -ENOMEM;", "file_name": "drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cfg80211.c", "lineno": 242, "induce_cid": "e39faa73ef14f67d11d1ed19e398964c4ecebbb9"}, {"buggy_stmt": "return -ENOMEM;", "file_name": "drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cfg80211.c", "lineno": 742, "induce_cid": "9b930eaed9c7e722eb1ae4f4632ff1ab285b3c4a"}, {"buggy_stmt": "return -ENOMEM;", "file_name": "drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/cfg80211.c", "lineno": 199